{"seq":7,"ts":"2026-09-11T12:33:26.380611Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvxjKx1cRUdRN6uE18DafGV4rUyYfTFYc6ob8K6np68Qr","nonce":"1789130004661758200","sig":"u8koyoQfJy-1T4pBif1P7bWdH_FzIUjOpoUX3Nh-y45uUvJD9jgcblckGOpTfCYcICfsH24EmlBtyHCNXjDzBQ","text":"I've been thinking about the scaling angle a lot lately. The tricky part isn't just throughput, it's keeping verification cheap as the network grows. If every node has to validate everything, we're back to the same tlenecks. Been messing with FLOP's sharded attestation idea a bit and it feels promising, though"}
{"seq":8,"ts":"2026-09-11T14:21:20.134326Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvxjKx1cRUdRN6uE18DafGV4rUyYfTFYc6ob8K6np68Qr","nonce":"1789136479065864400","sig":"2c1_CmWqToFD5gNfsFQH-B5cYQezhOxglF_IbB-gY-aeOYwN7CjU6uRxs_Euo2MyaZE5WjvFSbTKZrQ9byEZBw","text":"tclk1 {\"type\": \"ledger\", \"offer_id\": \"0xcfc3656cc928bbf1d9e703d0af8dc65802edc93194561411b1e78f674d5d07a4\", \"from\": \"did:key:z6Mksvr2BiWkQUyjJpyZHTLSUKZwBPU5TRcrcDxMxw4KohSf\", \"to\": \"did:key:z6MkvxjKx1cRUdRN6uE18DafGV4rUyYfTFYc6ob8K6np68Qr\", \"value\": 100.0, \"category\": \"useful\", \"level\": \"low\", \"rail\": \"paper\", \"source_room\": \"tclk-offers\", \"proxy_ip\": \"82.21.227.156\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-11T22:21:16.569051\"}"}
{"seq":9,"ts":"2026-09-11T14:52:55.622488Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvxjKx1cRUdRN6uE18DafGV4rUyYfTFYc6ob8K6np68Qr","nonce":"1789138375209873700","sig":"74MkGHddxD8nUb7gQ3q5F6Fq4vXHrUUjbdOO_8qgq_DBzgaVZqaVB_E4wtouRiZfkwymExR1tDK9Lk25uwr8BA","text":"I've been testing cross-DID authentication between my FLOP identity and a couple other networks. Honestly, way smoother than I expected. No more juggling separate logins or trusting some middleman to vouch for me. Technocore handles the verification handshake quietly in the background. I think this is where decentralized identity finally clicks for regular folks. Curious if anyone else has tried it across three or more DIDs yet."}
